Then I just became more
comfortable and realizing like,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.380
this is the only smile I got.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.460
So I'm just gonna try and
use it as much as I can.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.293
- [Thoraya] What do you think

00:01:38.293 --> 00:01:41.410
is the number one chronic
disease in America?

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.810
- Number one chronic disease,

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:44.980
depression.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.000
- Probably mental health.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.215
- In America or the world?

00:01:47.215 --> 00:01:48.048
- [Thoraya] America.

00:01:48.048 --> 00:01:49.150
- America, obesity.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.370
- Probably cardiovascular
disease, I would say.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:54.800
- I think that the major chronic
illness is heart disease.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.570
- [Thoraya] It's a good guess.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.313
It's actually tooth decay.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.580
- Wow.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.913
Okay, did not see that one coming.

00:02:02.913 --> 00:02:06.730
- Way off, I was way off, way off.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.200
- Tooth decay?

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.040
Oh.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.660
- [Thoraya] Is that
shocking at all, to hear?

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.860
- That's very shocking.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.810
It's definitely a reality
that people don't realize

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.540
and probably overlook that

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.920
having access to good, proper
dental care, is a privilege.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.670
And we are very lucky.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.950
Those of us that are able
to just have things like

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.040
toothpaste and toothbrushes and mouthwash

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.100
and everything else at our disposal.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.660
- I mean, man, if you think about it,

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.510
teeth are actually decaying
inside of your mouth.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.490
That's a disease for sure.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.570
People don't think about it

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.540
because I guess it's so
prevalent and nobody really,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.690
like, I can't say nobody cares,

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.260
but like, I don't know,
just lack of awareness.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.840
And, you know, when you
say the word ignorant,

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.330
it's not in any derogative sense

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.280
because I am very ignorant.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.740
I don't know how to
change my oil by myself.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.090
I'm ignorant on how to do so.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.170
So ignorance is the main reason

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.750
why people don't know that tooth decay

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.780
is the most prevalent disease.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.440
- I think there's probably less access

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.080
to affordable dental care.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.280
Primary care comes first,

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.570
but I think dental care is
probably an afterthought

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.403
for a lot of people.

00:03:09.403 --> 00:03:12.320
And I never went to the dentist as a child

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.749
because just in my family, you know,

00:03:13.749 --> 00:03:14.582
we didn't have a lot of money,

00:03:14.582 --> 00:03:15.690
so it was never a priority.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.720
You know, we didn't have a lot of money,

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:17.750
but we were broke.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.300
So if that was the case for me,

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.767
I can only imagine what
it's like for other families

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.357
that also didn't have that bandwidth.

00:03:23.357 --> 00:03:24.190
Yeah, it's something that I hope

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:27.790
that becomes more accessible
to more people as time goes on.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.070
- Maybe people are prioritizing things

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.790
more than dental care.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.260
If they only have like access

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.890
to a certain amount of resources.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.940
Maybe they are putting other things first

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.210
'cause they think that
that's more important

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.570
or they're maybe like putting it off.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.003
That's what I would think.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.240
- Hey, everyone Thoraya here.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.540
I think, and I'm sure we could all agree

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.170
that all smiles are beautiful,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.050
but it's about how we personally feel

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.440
about our smile and that matters most.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.200
And I'm not just talking about how we feel

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.720
about our smile visually,

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.350
but also the health of
our smile and oral health.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.440
Tooth decay is the number one
chronic disease in America.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.660
And no one is immune.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.200
Every American deserves a healthy smile,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.570
but Crest and Oral B know that

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:10.410
the opportunities to achieve
it, aren't always equal.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.900
This year Crest and Oral B are on mission

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.170
to make great oral health a reality

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.490
for everyone in America.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.750
And now I want you all to come with me

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.280
on a journey where we
will get to see firsthand

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.330
how Crest and Oral B are
helping make a positive change

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.630
by providing equitable
access to dental care,

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.637
education and products.

00:04:28.637 --> 00:04:29.470
(hands clap)

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.303
- Let's go.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.886
(upbeat music)

00:04:52.927 --> 00:04:54.660
- I think you should start with my story.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.970
And that leads into what I do.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.200
I grew up in a low-income household

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.070
and I had amazing parents who care for me,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.750
but unfortunately they
didn't know about oral health

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.520
or the importance of prevention.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.750
Nobody ever taught them or
educated them about those things.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.700
And so then in turn,
they didn't educate me.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.310
I didn't know that I should be brushing

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.880
or that I should be flossing

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.350
or about nutritional counseling.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.533
That I shouldn't eat all the candies.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.420
And so, as a consequence, I
had a lot of dental problems,

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.610
but because I was low income,

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:26.292
I didn't have access to dental care.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:29.709
(upbeat music continues)

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.850
The first time I went to a dentist,

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.600
I was probably around 13 years old.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:40.243
I was in such extreme pain,
that I couldn't sleep.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.563
This pain wouldn't go away.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.000
And my mom took me to a dentist.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.650
That dentist told my mom
that I needed a root canal

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.620
and my parents couldn't afford that.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.750
So instead my mom took me
home and she ground up cloves.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.010
She would mix it with water

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:00.253
and I would stick it into
the hole in my tooth.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.850
And then I would try
to sleep away the pain.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:06.890
And while the home remedies helped some,

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.433
it didn't help completely.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.573
So I just suffered through it.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.400
That memory is very vivid for me.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.060
I remember the sun being bright.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.720
I remember the green and yellow sheets.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.610
I know that I was laying at an angle,

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.350
is a very vivid memory for me.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.840
I'm pretty sure I had some
sort of periotreatment

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.260
because I remember as a young girl,

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:30.750
I would wake up in the morning

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.890
and there'd be blood on my pillow

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.630
and there'd be dried blood
on the corners of my mouth

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.423
and my mouth would be sick.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.760
But that stopped happening
after I received my dental care.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.110
And I made that connection.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.360
Since then, I've become
a dental hygienist.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.320
The first one in my family
to graduate from college.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.930
And I chose dental hygiene.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.710
I've organized around 40
community outreach events,

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.050
and these events are
free to the community.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.750
We do free oral cancer screenings,

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.050
free instruments, education,

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.520
because I truly believe
in the power of education

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.380
in offering people resources

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.410
and letting them know the
resources available to them.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.750
- [Thoraya] So how has
it been working with

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.650
Crest and Oral B?

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.800
How did you start working with them?

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.910
- Yeah, Crest and Oral B's been amazing

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.060
through my story of access to care.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.000
They've supported me and
in my entire journey,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.920
in my vocal Latinidad,

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.990
they've supported me in being a minority

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:29.130
and being strong and outspoken,

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:29.963
and I love that.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.430
But it's really made an
impact in my community.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.240
They've provided me with free products

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.550
to give to my patients.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.190
Things that I otherwise in our clinic

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.570
doesn't have resources
to sometimes purchase.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:45.570
And so through them, not
only are they supplying us

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.300
with things which might seem
minimal for our patients

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.260
who don't have resources,

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:50.170
who don't have money,

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.300
it makes an impact for them.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.860
Because otherwise they wouldn't
have access to these things.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.790
We ask the children, if
they have a toothbrush

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.060
before we ask them if they're brushing,

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.560
because a lot of children
don't have toothbrushes.

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.210
I didn't have a toothbrush growing up.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:05.650
You know, there was
probably things around,

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.260
but nothing doesn't mean to me.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.150
And we've learned that in our communities,

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.300
it's so easy to assume that everybody

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.650
has the same resources that we do.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.500
And that's not the reality.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.710
Maybe it's our reality,

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:18.830
but it's not the reality for the majority

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.130
of the United States.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:23.820
We talk about cavities being
the number one chronic disease.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.653
What does that tell you?

00:08:24.653 --> 00:08:26.920
That tells you that there's
a disparities happening.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:29.487
And that's not just me and my experiences

00:08:29.487 --> 00:08:32.200
there are statistics and
studies that show that.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.490
You mentioned earlier, like

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.290
when was the last time your cheeks hurt?

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:36.123
My cheeks hurt right now,

00:08:36.123 --> 00:08:37.940
just talking about Crest and Oral B,

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:40.170
because I am really appreciative to them.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:42.390
And the support that
they've given not just me,

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:46.760
but my patients, and, you
know, as a big company,

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.760
like Crest and Oral they
don't have to do those things.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:50.873
And yet they do.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:54.130
And I don't see any other company

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.550
out there doing those things.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:57.880
Yeah, they took an interest in me and I,

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.760
and I don't necessarily feel like I bring

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.920
that much value to them.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.083
But they definitely bring
value to me and to my patients.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:09.270
I didn't want to cry.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.550
They choose to highlight
communities that are suffering,

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:17.920
communities that do need advocacy,

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.933
communities that are often overlooked.

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:23.210
That's says a lot to me.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.190
I think when we think about dental care

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:29.110
and how we take it for granted

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.250
and we're dealing with these children

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.870
and we think that their
lives are so simple.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:36.050
Their lives aren't simple,
their lives are complicated.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.860
We want to provide them with
education and resources.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.220
We're there to help them.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.510
And if we're not there to help them,

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.610
then we don't need to be there.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:47.010
And I truly believe that.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.030
I am not their savior.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:48.870
We are not their savior.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:49.950
What we're doing is important,

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:52.040
but it's one thing that we're doing.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.100
And so if we're not there to do the good,

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:54.933
then we shouldn't be there.

00:09:54.933 --> 00:09:56.050
And I think that we are.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:58.733
I don't know.

00:09:58.733 --> 00:10:01.373
I just, I keep thinking back on how,

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.470
I kind of imagined this for myself,

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:09.017
being that child who was
laying in a bed, in pain,

00:10:09.017 --> 00:10:10.213
unable to sleep,

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:15.970
and now to be partnering
with Crest and Oral B,

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:19.800
to bring access to care,
to children like me,

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.790
to people like my parents,

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:24.473
like my grandparents,

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.890
what a better life.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.490
And I'm truly grateful
that Crest and Oral B

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.540
that they are supporting me in my mission

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:33.720
in caring for the community

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:38.350
in turning a little girl's
suffering into a mission

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:39.580
so that other children don't have

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:40.980
to suffer these same things.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:45.327
(upbeat music continues)

